-- Round 72 (Track D). TARGET: literature closure for H2 + a sourced echo.
-- lambda_C identified: the classical Lagarias-Weiss branching model in
-- C-parametrization gives x^2 = x + 1/3, lambda = (1+sqrt(7/3))/2 =
-- 1.26376; three computations agree (tree 1.2637, automaton 1.26355,
-- closed form). Applegate-Lagarias (Experimental Math 4, 1995) report real
-- trees vary "significantly narrower" than the branching model — the same
-- mild sub-random regularity Track D measured in kicks and slices: the
-- suppression is a DOCUMENTED, unexplained feature of the problem.
